Title: 0008-aros-fileselector-parent-null
Repository: grafx2
Base-Commit: f84cb09dc59d706d6e7b28778b01ba911f52298c
Requires: 0007-aros-renderer-no-sticky-hint.patch
Author: aros-grafx2 project
Date: 2026-09-20
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: AROS and other Amiga-family targets where PARENT_DIR is /. NULL-safe strdup is generic; the / mapping is Amiga-only.

Problem:
  Load/Save fileselector: PARENT_DIR is / on AROS, POSIX chdir(/) fails, then a NULL filename is stolen and the next scroll does strdup(NULL) which AROS strlen treats as illegal address 0x80000003. Same crash after clicking the name field on a directory (filename is NULLed on purpose).
Solution:
  Map Amiga parent / to chdir(..) on AROS/Amiga. Reject NULL Change_directory. Do not strdup or strcmp a NULL filename in Scroll_fileselector and the other Load/Save strdup sites; skip empty chdir and restore a list item instead of stealing NULL.
Validation:
  2026-09-21: ABIv11 build and QEMU one regression. See docs/attachments/2026-09-21-fileselector/REPORT.md.
  Patch 0008 alone stops the NULL crash; parent navigation requires patch 0009.
Removal:
  Keep until equivalent upstream fixes replace the guarded selection and AROS parent-path handling.

